      "side": 1,
      "message": "After this change invoke_restperfclient is called from nowhere but this wrapper, yet it stays public with the more obvious name — so the next suite is likely to call it and quietly lose its log on failure, which is the bug this change fixes. Could the try/finally copy move into invoke_restperfclient itself (dropping this wrapper), or invoke_restperfclient become _invoke_restperfclient?",
